# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js portfolio project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` using pnpm
- Package added to dependencies in `package.json`
- Lock file (`pnpm-lock.yaml`) updated with new dependency tree

### 2. Code Changes
**File: `src/app/layout.js`**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag (after `<SpeedInsights />`)
- Placement follows Next.js App Router best practices from official documentation

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
- Identified as Next.js 15.5.28 with App Router
- Using JavaScript (not TypeScript) for the root layout
- Package manager: pnpm v10.34.5

### Documentation Reference
Fetched latest instructions from: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Confirmed package name: `@vercel/analytics`
- Followed Next.js App Router specific implementation
- Analytics component placed in root layout for global tracking

### Build Verification
- Build tested successfully (required temporary Appwrite env vars for unrelated dependency)
- No linting or compilation errors introduced by Analytics changes
- Component properly integrated alongside existing SpeedInsights component

## Next Steps for Deployment
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel Dashboard (Analytics sidebar → Enable button)
2. Deploy to Vercel to activate tracking
3. Verify tracking by checking browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*` routes

## Files Modified
- `portfolio/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `portfolio/pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `portfolio/src/app/layout.js` - Added Analytics component import and usage

## Notes
- Analytics component is a client-side component that will automatically track page views
- No additional configuration required
- Works seamlessly with existing SpeedInsights implementation
- Zero impact on existing functionality or code structure
